[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Petrov's Defense"]
[Variation "Petrov's Defense: Damiano Variation"]
[ECO "C42"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "trap,queen-trap"]
[Themes "discovered-check"]
[Refutes "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 Nxe4"]
[Kind "for-us"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. Nxe5 Nxe4?! { Black grabs the pawn at once, which is the most natural mistake in the Petrov. It walks into a pin along the e-file. } 4. Qe2 { Attacks the knight on e4, which is pinned: if it moves, the white knight on e5 uncovers a check from the queen. } 4... Nf6? { Looks natural, but moving the knight uncovers the queen's line to the king. } 5. Nc6+ { Discovered check from the queen, and the knight on c6 also attacks the black queen. Black must answer the check and loses the queen. } 5... Qe7 6. Nxe7 Bxe7 *
